          "file": "app/presentation/unit_testing.rb",
          "from": "caption: \"Readme\\r\\n\" +\n    \"==============\\r\\n\" +\n    \"\\r\\n\" +\n    \"Configuration\\r\\n\" +\n    \"-------------------------------------\\r\\n\" +\n    \"Do not modify this module, instead\\r\\n\" +\n    \"1. Create a new custom module (e.g. UnitTests)\\r\\n\" +\n    \"2. Download the CommunityCommons module from the App Store, when you don't already have it available in your project.\\r\\n\" +\n    \"3. Call 'UnitTestOverview' microflow, which calls the java action looking for available tests and opens the overview page.\\r\\n\" +\n    \"4. You can also choose to copy the snippet UnitTestOverview to a (new) page the new custom module\\r\\n\" +\n    \"Make sure the java action 'FindAllUnitTests' is called before the new page with the snippet is opened. The java action checks the model for 'unit test' microflows/ java actions. \\r\\n\" +\n    \"5. Take a look at the examples in the 'Example Tests' folder. Use these examples as a pointer to create your own unit tests.\\r\\n\" +\n    \"6. Your custom unit tests need to be prefixed with case-insensitive 'Test_' or 'UT_' in order to be picked up automatically by this unit test module.\\r\\n\" +\n    \"\\r\\n\"",
